Add StGit overlay workflow

Purpose: keep the fork's features as a StGit patch stack on top of
upstream main, so they replay onto every new upstream release and can
be shared, reviewed and landed through GitHub.

Approach: OVERLAY.md documents the branches (main mirrors upstream,
overlay carries the stack), updating, patch descriptions and the
topic-stack review flow. tools/ holds the git side that .git/config
cannot version: overlay-setup.sh (remotes, stack ref fetch spec,
aliases), overlay-publish.sh (atomic push of branch + stack ref),
overlay-adopt.sh (copy a published stack into local overlay).

Constraints: stack refs are fetched into refs/remote-stacks/origin/*,
never refs/stacks/*, so a fetch cannot overwrite local stack work.
Scripts keep LF endings (tools/.gitattributes).
